# Feature MODULE.md

## Why

Each feature keeps a **MODULE.md** next to its API barrel so humans and agents share one short map of domain wiring, ports, and drift anchors—without duplicating code.

## Where the template lives

- **Blank copy-paste body:** `.cursor/skills/module-documentation/reference.md`
- **When to create/update and drift rules:** `.cursor/skills/module-documentation/SKILL.md`

Do **not** paste the full template into this rule; the skill is canonical.

## Business rules (mandatory policy)

- **Never assume** product or domain rules (pricing, fees, surcharges, channels, eligibility, money, compliance). Do **not** add or imply **## Business rules [VERIFY]** content from inference, “typical POS behaviour”, or other apps.
- **Only** document a business rule when it is **explicitly stated or confirmed by a developer** (conversation, ticket, review). If unclear, **ask** before encoding rules in MODULE.md or code.
- Once written under **Business rules [VERIFY]**, treat them as **drift-sensitive**: code changes that contradict the table require an intentional doc update and should align with developer intent.

## What belongs in MODULE.md

- **At a glance, purpose & boundaries, lifecycle** (or N/A with reason)
- **Business rules [VERIFY]** — optional section; **only** developer-confirmed rules (see above); omit entirely if none apply or none are confirmed
- **Ports (incoming)** and **adapters (outgoing)** — behavioural contracts and type names, not every `ref.watch`
- **Side effects** downstream (state, bus, persistence) when that is the module’s job
- **Entry points [VERIFY]** — only section that must list concrete **paths** to barrel, DI, module
- **Progressive disclosure** — numbered list with **paths** into handlers/module/DI; then package-level pointers without file paths
- Prefer **typed AppEvents** as documented ports over unexplained Riverpod/stream side effects

## What does not belong

- **UI** (widgets, screens, routes UX): not MODULE.md; a future **FEATURE.md** may cover that
- **Assumed business rules** — if not confirmed, do not document as fact
- Boilerplate only (**Logger**, generic providers) unless behaviourally part of the contract
- File paths outside **Entry points** and **Progressive disclosure**

## When working here

If you change **module init**, **handlers**, **DI**, **event subscriptions**, **core behaviour**, **what the feature owns**, or **developer-confirmed business rules**, update **MODULE.md** in the same change (or follow up immediately) so `[VERIFY]` and tables stay true.
